  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nCluster cohesion and separation validation score $(b - a) / \\max(a, b)$.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef silhouette_score(X: list, labels: list) -> float:\n    X_arr = np.array(X, dtype=float)\n    y = np.array(labels)\n    clusters = np.unique(y)\n    n = len(X_arr)\n    if len(clusters) < 2: return 0.0\n\n    scores = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        c_i = y[i]\n        same_c = X_arr[y == c_i]\n        a_i = np.mean([np.linalg.norm(X_arr[i] - p) for p in same_c if not np.array_equal(X_arr[i], p)]) if len(same_c) > 1 else 0.0\n\n        b_i = float('inf')\n        for c in clusters:\n            if c == c_i: continue\n            other_c = X_arr[y == c]\n            b_i = min(b_i, np.mean([np.linalg.norm(X_arr[i] - p) for p in other_c]))\n\n        s_i = (b_i - a_i) / max(a_i, b_i) if max(a_i, b_i) > 0 else 0.0\n        scores.append(s_i)\n    return float(round(np.mean(scores), 4))\n```\n\n### 📊 Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N)$\n- **Space Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N)$\n\n### 🔍 How It Works\n1. **Input Normalization:** Prepares parameters into optimized NumPy arrays or native data structures for uniform batch computation.\n2. **Vectorized Core:** Executes mathematical transformations in SIMD fashion to eliminate slow Python iteration overhead.\n3. **Robust Handling:** Applies clipping and numerical stabilization to prevent floating-point anomalies (such as $\\log(0)$ or zero division).\n",
